# Voter Slip Print System - Complete Documentation

## Overview

The voter slip print system has been completely rewritten to use **Node.js with Puppeteer** instead of Python. This eliminates the Python dependency and provides a fully configurable, easy-to-customize solution.

**Status:** ✅ **COMPLETE AND WORKING**

---

## What Changed

### ❌ Old System (Deprecated)
- **Technology:** Python + WeasyPrint
- **Issues:** 
  - Python not found error on user's system
  - Hardcoded layout with no configuration options
  - Difficult to customize
  - External dependency management

### ✅ New System (Current)
- **Technology:** Node.js + Puppeteer + HTML/CSS
- **Benefits:**
  - No Python dependency required
  - Fully configurable layout, fonts, margins, colors
  - Easy to customize without code changes
  - Better error handling and logging
  - Multiple slip layouts per page support

---

## System Architecture

### Core Files

#### 1. **server/printSlipConfig.ts** - Configuration Management
The single source of truth for all print slip customization.

```typescript
interface PrintSlipConfig {
  page: {
    width: 210;        // A4 width (mm)
    height: 297;       // A4 height (mm)
    slipsPerPage: 2;   // Slips per page (2 = 2 rows, each 105×148.5mm)
  };
  
  slip: {
    width: 105;        // Single slip width
    height: 148.5;     // Single slip height
    padding: 5;        // Internal padding
    margin: 2;         // Border margin
    backgroundColor: '#ffffff';
    borderColor: '#000000';
    borderWidth: 1;    // px
  };
  
  header: {
    showHeaderImage: true;
    logoHeight: 20;    // mm
    logoWidth: 20;     // mm
    logoPosition: { top: 3, left: 3 };
  };
  
  title: {
    text: 'VOTER SLIP';
    fontSize: 14;      // pt
    fontWeight: 'bold';
    color: '#000000';
    marginBottom: 2;   // mm
    textAlign: 'center';
  };
  
  subtitle: {
    text: 'Election Commission';
    fontSize: 9;
    fontWeight: 'normal';
    color: '#333333';
    marginBottom: 3;
    textAlign: 'center';
  };
  
  fields: [
    {
      label: 'Name';
      dataKey: 'Name';           // MongoDB field name
      fontSize: 10;              // pt
      fontWeight: 'bold';
      labelWidth: 22;            // mm (width of label text)
      marginBottom: 2;           // mm
      marginLeft: 3;             // mm (indent from left)
      showLabel: true;
      columnsInLine?: 2;         // 1 or 2 fields per line
    },
    // ... more fields
  ];
  
  footer: {
    text: 'Please carry your Identity Card';
    fontSize: 8;
    fontWeight: 'normal';
    color: '#666666';
    textAlign: 'center';
    marginTop: 2;              // mm
    borderTop: true;
    borderTopColor: '#cccccc';
  };
  
  font: {
    family: 'Devanagari, Arial, sans-serif';
    baseSize: 11;              // pt
  };
  
  print: {
    orientation: 'portrait';
    margins: { top: 5, right: 5, bottom: 5, left: 5 }; // mm
  };
}
```

**Location:** `server/printSlipConfig.ts`
**Usage:** Import and modify for customization

---

#### 2. **server/printSlipGenerator.ts** - HTML Generation
Converts configuration and voter data into HTML suitable for PDF conversion.

**Key Methods:**

```typescript
// Generate HTML for a single slip
generator.generateSlipHTML(voter: any, logoDataUrl?: string): string

// Generate HTML for multiple slips (e.g., 4 per A4)
generator.generatePrintHTML(voters: any[], logoDataUrl?: string): string

// Generate HTML for a single page
generator.generatePageHTML(votersGroup: any[], logoDataUrl?: string): string
```

**Features:**
- Automatic field layout based on configuration
- Support for 1 or 2 column layouts per line
- Graceful fallbacks for missing data (shows "-")
- Support for logo/header images via data URLs
- Automatic indentation and spacing

---

#### 3. **server/pdfService.ts** - PDF Generation
Converts HTML to PDF using Puppeteer (headless Chrome).

**Key Functions:**

```typescript
// Generate PDF from HTML
async generatePDFFromHTML(
  htmlContent: string,
  outputPath: string,
  options?: {
    width?: string;
    height?: string;
    margin?: { top?: string; ... };
  }
): Promise<string>

// Generate PDF for single voter
async generateVoterSlipPDF(
  voter: any,
  outputPath: string,
  htmlGenerator: (voter: any) => string
): Promise<string>

// Generate PDF with multiple slips
async generateMultipleSlipsPDF(
  voters: any[],
  outputPath: string,
  htmlGenerator: (voters: any[]) => string
): Promise<string>
```

**Features:**
- Automatic browser instance management (reuses browser for efficiency)
- A4 paper size support
- Full color printing support
- Automatic page breaks for multiple pages
- Memory-efficient (single-process mode)
- Automatic cleanup on process exit

---

#### 4. **server/routes.ts** - API Endpoint
New `POST /api/voters/:id/print` endpoint for generating and downloading PDFs.

**Request:**
```http
POST /api/voters/507f1f77bcf86cd799439011/print
Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>
```

**Response:**
- Success: PDF file download
- Error: JSON with error message

**Code:**
```typescript
app.post(api.voters.printSlip.path, requireAuth, async (req, res) => {
  const voter = await storage.getVoter(req.params.id);
  const generator = createPrintSlipGenerator();
  const htmlContent = generator.generateSlipHTML(voter);
  
  // Generate PDF
  const pdfPath = path.join(tempDir, `slip-${voter._id}-${Date.now()}.pdf`);
  await generatePDFFromHTML(htmlContent, pdfPath);
  
  // Send to client
  res.contentType("application/pdf");
  res.setHeader("Content-Disposition", `attachment; filename="voter-slip-${voter._id}.pdf"`);
  fs.createReadStream(pdfPath).pipe(res);
});
```

